---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="For Organizations | Ethnoir"
  description="Examine whether entrepreneurship support fits participant needs and translate evidence into practical decisions about design, delivery and measurement."
>
  <!-- SECTION 1: OPENING INSTITUTIONAL BRIEF -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter" style="padding-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, var(--space-2xl)); padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, var(--space-2xl)); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);">
        <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-muted-slate); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em;">For Organizations</span>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Dominant Masterhead -->
      <div style="margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, var(--space-2xl)); max-width: 1040px;">
        <h1 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5.5vw, 4.25rem); margin: 0; line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">
          Support works better when it fits the people it is meant to serve.
        </h1>
      </div>
      
      <!-- Introductory Synthesis & Immediate Action Group -->
      <div class="grid-12" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary); padding-top: var(--space-lg); align-items: start;">
        <div class="col-12 lg-col-8">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: clamp(1.1875rem, 2vw, 1.35rem); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
            An organization may offer useful support that participants struggle to access, apply or sustain. The next decision could concern the support itself, its timing, the delivery process or the evidence available. Ethnoir works with organizations that support entrepreneurs to examine these questions and translate what they learn into practical changes.
          </p>
          <div class="actions-group" style="margin-top: 0;">
            <a href="/contact?type=institutional" class="btn-primary" style="background-color: var(--color-tidal-ink); color: var(--color-porcelain); text-decoration: none;">
              Discuss an entrepreneurship-support challenge
            </a>
            <a href="/our-work" class="link-secondary voice-3" style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-weight: 600;">
              View Our Work &rarr;
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 2: TARGET AUDIENCE LEDGER / WHO THIS IS FOR -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid-12" style="align-items: center;">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15;">
            Who this is for
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-8">
          <div style="background-color: var(--color-parchment); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-deep-teal); padding: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 2rem); border: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); border-left-width: 3px; border-left-color: var(--color-deep-teal);">
            <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
              Entrepreneurship-support organizations, universities, foundations, nonprofits, public agencies and others whose programs, funding or resources shape how people start, run or change a business. You do not need to be a business.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 3: INQUIRY DIALOGUE / QUESTIONS ORGANIZATIONS BRING (COMPACT) -->
  <section class="bg-quiet-sand chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid-12">
        <div class="col-12 lg-col-4" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0;">
            Questions organizations bring
          </h2>
        </div>
        
        <div class="col-12 lg-col-8">
          <div class="grid-12" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
            <div class="col-12 md-col-6 border-right-md" style="padding: clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem) clamp(0rem, 1.5vw, var(--space-md)) clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
              <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.4vw, 1.2rem); line-height: 1.4; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-style: italic;">
                What are the founders we serve dealing with, and how does that compare with what our support assumes?
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-12 md-col-6" style="padding: clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem) 0 clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem) clamp(0rem, 1.5vw, var(--space-md)); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
              <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.4vw, 1.2rem); line-height: 1.4; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-style: italic;">
                Where do people get confused, drop out or struggle to apply what is offered?
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-12 md-col-6 border-right-md" style="padding: clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem) clamp(0rem, 1.5vw, var(--space-md)) clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
              <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.4vw, 1.2rem); line-height: 1.4; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-style: italic;">
                Would a change to the support, its sequence or its delivery process address the issue?
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-12 md-col-6" style="padding: clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem) 0 clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem) clamp(0rem, 1.5vw, var(--space-md)); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule);">
              <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.4vw, 1.2rem); line-height: 1.4; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-style: italic;">
                When might a referral be appropriate, and what would make the handoff workable?
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-12" style="padding: clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem) 0;">
              <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.4vw, 1.2rem); line-height: 1.4; margin: 0; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-style: italic;">
                What evidence would help us decide what to retain, change or stop?
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 4: DELIVERABLES & SCOPE / WHAT AN AGREED ENGAGEMENT COULD PRODUCE (COMPACT) -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid-12">
        <div class="col-12 lg-col-5" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
            What an agreed engagement could produce
          </h2>
        </div>
        
        <div class="col-12 lg-col-7">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
            Depending on the question, available evidence and agreed scope, the work could produce:
          </p>
          
          <!-- Interactive Deliverables Accordion -->
          <div class="deliverables-accordion" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
            <details open style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); padding: 4px 0;">
              <summary class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 10px 0; list-style: none;">
                <span style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
                  <span style="color: var(--color-deep-teal); font-weight: 700;">&mdash;</span>
                  <span>Decision brief</span>
                </span>
                <span class="accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true">&plus;</span>
              </summary>
              <div style="padding: 2px 0 10px 22px;">
                <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; color: var(--color-deep-body);">
                  A short decision brief setting out the question, findings, evidence gaps and recommended next steps.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); padding: 4px 0;">
              <summary class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 10px 0; list-style: none;">
                <span style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
                  <span style="color: var(--color-deep-teal); font-weight: 700;">&mdash;</span>
                  <span>Participant journey map</span>
                </span>
                <span class="accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true">&plus;</span>
              </summary>
              <div style="padding: 2px 0 10px 22px;">
                <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; color: var(--color-deep-body);">
                  A map of the participant journey, showing where needs, entry requirements, activities or handoffs may not align.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); padding: 4px 0;">
              <summary class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 10px 0; list-style: none;">
                <span style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
                  <span style="color: var(--color-deep-teal); font-weight: 700;">&mdash;</span>
                  <span>Revised support outline &amp; workflow</span>
                </span>
                <span class="accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true">&plus;</span>
              </summary>
              <div style="padding: 2px 0 10px 22px;">
                <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; color: var(--color-deep-body);">
                  A revised support outline or delivery workflow, including activities, materials, responsibilities and referral handoffs where relevant.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); padding: 4px 0;">
              <summary class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 10px 0; list-style: none;">
                <span style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
                  <span style="color: var(--color-deep-teal); font-weight: 700;">&mdash;</span>
                  <span>Measurement and follow-up plan</span>
                </span>
                <span class="accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true">&plus;</span>
              </summary>
              <div style="padding: 2px 0 10px 22px;">
                <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; color: var(--color-deep-body);">
                  A measurement and follow-up plan defining what to examine, when and how findings will inform decisions.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>

          <!-- Bounding Scope Callout -->
          <div style="background-color: var(--color-parchment); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-tidal-ink); padding: clamp(0.875rem, 1.5vw, 1.25rem); border: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); border-left-width: 3px; border-left-color: var(--color-tidal-ink);">
            <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
              An initial conversation establishes the question, fit and possible scope. Substantive analysis, design, implementation and written deliverables belong in a separately agreed engagement. The appropriate response may be a change to an existing service, a clearer handoff, a revised support sequence or a new founder-facing program.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 5: SUPPORT FIT FRAMEWORK / WHY EXAMINE SUPPORT FIT -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter chapter-large-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid-12" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-5">
          <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15; margin: 0;">
            Why examine support fit
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-7">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: clamp(1.1875rem, 2vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
            Examining support fit gives an organization a clearer basis for deciding where to focus staff time, funding and specialist input.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 3-Column Comparative Analytical Grid -->
      <div class="grid-12" style="background-color: var(--color-porcelain); border: 1px solid var(--color-quiet-rule); border-top: 3px solid var(--color-tidal-ink);">
        
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 border-right-md" style="padding: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
          <h3 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">
            Relevance
          </h3>
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
            Examine whether the support offered addresses the situations and priorities of the people expected to use it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 border-right-md" style="padding: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
          <h3 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">
            Usability
          </h3>
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
            Consider whether timing, entry requirements, workload and handoffs make the support practical to access and apply.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="padding: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
          <h3 class="voice-1" style="font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);">
            Decision-making
          </h3>
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
            Define what evidence will help the organization decide what to retain, adjust or stop.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 6: PROOF POINT / THE VENTURE READINESS LAB -->
  <section class="bg-porcelain chapter chapter-large-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid-12" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-5">
          <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15; margin: 0;">
            The Venture Readiness Lab
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-7">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: clamp(1.1875rem, 2vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
            In 2026 Ethnoir designed and delivered a six-week pilot for founders. Six active founders reached the final session. Five had structural business deliverables that Ethnoir’s Founder reviewed and confirmed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Architectural Fact Strip -->
      <div class="grid-12" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary); margin-bottom: var(--space-xl); background-color: var(--color-parchment);">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 border-right-md" style="padding: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);">
          <div class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 4rem); line-height: 1; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); font-style: italic;">
            6
          </div>
          <div class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-weight: 500;">
            weeks
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 border-right-md" style="padding: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);">
          <div class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 4rem); line-height: 1; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); font-style: italic;">
            6
          </div>
          <div class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-weight: 500;">
            active founders
          </div>
          <div class="voice-3" style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate); margin: 4px 0 0 0; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: normal;">
            reached the final session
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="padding: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);">
          <div class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 4rem); line-height: 1; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); font-style: italic;">
            5
          </div>
          <div class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-weight: 500;">
            deliverables
          </div>
          <div class="voice-3" style="font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-muted-slate); margin: 4px 0 0 0; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: normal;">
            reviewed and confirmed by the Founder
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-12" style="align-items: center;">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-8">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin: 0;">
            The Lab shows how Ethnoir connected a shared learning sequence with practical work on each founder’s business. The case explains the design, delivery, participant-created outputs and evidence.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="text-align: right;">
          <a href="/our-work/venture-readiness-lab" class="btn-primary" style="background-color: var(--color-tidal-ink); color: var(--color-porcelain); text-decoration: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;">
            <span>Explore the Venture Readiness Lab</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 7: FOUNDER BACKGROUND / EXPERIENCE BEHIND THE WORK -->
  <section class="bg-parchment chapter chapter-moderate-spacing" style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-strong-boundary);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid-12" style="align-items: center;">
        <div class="col-12 md-col-5" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-md);">
          <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 2.75rem); color: var(--color-tidal-ink); line-height: 1.15;">
            Experience behind the work
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 md-col-7">
          <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-deep-body); margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);">
            Ethnoir is led by Olajumoke Michael, whose experience includes program implementation with Bpeace and regional program leadership at the Winston-Salem Women’s Business Center. As U.S. Program Manager for Bpeace’s Breaking the $1M Barrier program, she coordinated delivery across North Carolina and Georgia, created guidance for coaches and facilitators, designed and facilitated peer-learning sessions, and shaped onboarding and Showcase preparation. At the Women’s Business Center, she led programming, fundraising, partnerships and improvements to client-service and reporting systems.
          </p>
          <div>
            <a
              href="https://olajumokemichael.com/experience/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="link-secondary voice-3"
              style="font-size: 1rem; color: var(--color-tidal-ink); font-weight: 600; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;"
            >
              <span>Explore her professional experience and selected work</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 8: WORKING WITH ETHNOIR -->
  <section class="bg-tidal-ink chapter chapter-large-spacing">
    <div class="container">
      
      <div style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl); max-width: 860px;">
        <h2 class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4.5vw, 3.5rem); color: var(--color-porcelain); margin-bottom: var(--space-md); letter-spacing: -0.02em;">
          Working with Ethnoir
        </h2>
        <p class="voice-1" style="font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.45rem); line-height: 1.4; color: var(--color-porcelain); margin-bottom: var(--space-sm); font-style: italic;">
          Start with the question you need to resolve.
        </p>
        <p class="voice-2" style="font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-parchment); margin: 0;">
          Ethnoir works with organizations on how entrepreneurship support is designed, delivered and improved. Bring a question about participant needs, access, delivery or measurement. You do not need a finished project brief.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- 3 Steps Grid on Dark (No Numbers) -->
      <div class="grid-12" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2); margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);">
        
        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 border-right-md" style="padding: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);">
          <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-quiet-sand); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); display: block; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">Tell us what needs attention</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-parchment); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
            Describe who your support serves, what is proving difficult and the decision you need to make.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 md-col-4 border-right-md" style="padding: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);">
          <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-quiet-sand); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); display: block; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">Explore the fit</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-parchment); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
            Together, we clarify the question, the information available and where Ethnoir could contribute.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="col-12 md-col-4" style="padding: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);">
          <span class="voice-3" style="color: var(--color-quiet-sand); margin-bottom: var(--space-xs); display: block; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em;">Define the next step</span>
          <p class="voice-2" style="color: var(--color-parchment); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0;">
